> I really want this feature too!

this works for me https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pull/32381
have to add `"experimental": {
    "log_messages": "trace"
  }` to `~/.opencode/opencode.json` and add env variable `OPENCODE_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG`, or start opencode with `OPENCODE_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG opencode`

Adding another concrete use case for this feature:

**Problem**: I registered an MCP tool (CodeGraph) that provides structured code querying — function definitions, class hierarchies, caller/callee relationships, impact analysis. It is objectively better than `grep` for these tasks. I wrote detailed instructions in AGENTS.md preferring CodeGraph over grep for structural queries.

But the model still reaches for `grep` every time. The root cause is exactly what this issue describes: the built-in `grep` tool has a hardcoded description that the model sees on every inference call, while my AGENTS.md preference is just text loaded once at session start — far from the tool selection decision point.

**What I need**: The ability to append to (not replace) a built-in tool's description at the project level, something like:

```jsonc
{
  "toolDescriptions": {
    "grep": {
      "append": "For structured code queries (function definitions, class hierarchies, caller/callee relationships, import graphs), prefer codegraph_search or codegraph_explore."
    }
  }
}
```

This would let the model see my preference right at the moment it chooses which tool to call, without conflicting with the original description.

The `replace` use case (gh → glab) and the `append` use case (MCP tool routing) are two sides of the same capability — letting users influence tool descriptions at the project level.

@VasyaYovbak — following up on your note that this PR got too big to review: I've split the workflow feature into a clean, **stacked series of 6 focused PRs** off `dev`, each reviewable on its own. The 4,810-line `workflow.ts` is modularized, and unrelated drift (the HTML-escape refactor, version bumps, stats) is dropped. Your `ctx.tool(...)` + plugin-registration work is included as layer 5.

Starting with **#32390** (engine-core, 1/6) now; the rest follow one-by-one as each merges — that's the only way to get clean *incremental* diffs, since cross-fork stacking can't show them otherwise.

How would you like to coordinate? Happy to keep #29789 open as the umbrella while the stack lands, or you can close it in favor of the split — whatever you prefer. Thanks again for being easy to work with!
